  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(x\\lt0,\\) then which of the following must be positive?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{x}{|x|}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-x^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(-2^x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(-x^{-1}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\sqrt[3]{x}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2010-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Choice (D) is \\(-x^{-1}=-\\dfrac1x.\\) When \\(x\\lt0,\\) \\(\\dfrac1x\\lt0,\\) so \\(-\\dfrac1x\\gt0.\\)\n\nTesting \\(x=-1\\) shows the other choices need not be positive: \\(\\dfrac{x}{|x|}=-1,\\) \\(-x^2=-1,\\) \\(-2^x=-\\tfrac12,\\) and \\(\\sqrt[3]{x}=-1.\\)\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Test each choice with a negative value such as \\(x=-1\\)",
        "Rewrite \\(-x^{-1}\\) as \\(-\\dfrac1x;\\) dividing into a negative number flips the sign"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
